  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{12+10}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{11} \\\\ \\frac{19}{22}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
